WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.153
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.453 --> 00:00:09.222
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.522 --> 00:00:14.450
Unit nineteen: Discourse Connectors. Today you will link ideas in formal writing.

4
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.321
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:21.441
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:23.168
Furthermore.

7
00:00:24.183 --> 00:00:26.647
Furthermore means adds a point to what you said.

8
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:28.669
Furthermore, it is cheap.

9
00:00:29.283 --> 00:00:32.052
Your turn. Say: Furthermore.

10
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:35.971
Furthermore.

11
00:00:36.717 --> 00:00:37.892
Nevertheless.

12
00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:41.057
Nevertheless means in spite of that.

13
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.383
Nevertheless, we continued.

14
00:00:43.983 --> 00:00:47.030
Your turn. Say: Nevertheless.

15
00:00:49.867 --> 00:00:51.262
Nevertheless.

16
00:00:52.017 --> 00:00:53.041
Consequently.

17
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.142
Consequently means as a result.

18
00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:58.401
Consequently, he failed.

19
00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:01.785
Your turn. Say: Consequently.

20
00:01:04.633 --> 00:01:05.762
Consequently.

21
00:01:06.517 --> 00:01:07.553
In addition.

22
00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.190
In addition means also.

23
00:01:10.783 --> 00:01:12.597
In addition, it is safe.

24
00:01:13.183 --> 00:01:15.650
Your turn. Say: In addition.

25
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.640
In addition.

26
00:01:20.383 --> 00:01:21.605
On the other hand.

27
00:01:22.617 --> 00:01:25.731
On the other hand means used to give a contrasting point.

28
00:01:26.317 --> 00:01:28.177
On the other hand, it's costly.

29
00:01:28.783 --> 00:01:31.436
Your turn. Say: On the other hand.

30
00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.603
On the other hand.

31
00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:37.328
Moreover.

32
00:01:38.317 --> 00:01:40.107
Moreover means what is more.

33
00:01:40.717 --> 00:01:42.565
Moreover, it saves time.

34
00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.675
Your turn. Say: Moreover.

35
00:01:48.533 --> 00:01:49.523
Moreover.

36
00:01:50.283 --> 00:01:51.238
Cohesion.

37
00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.004
Cohesion means how a text holds together.

38
00:01:55.617 --> 00:01:56.792
Good cohesion.

39
00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.001
Your turn. Say: Cohesion.

40
00:02:02.867 --> 00:02:03.914
Cohesion.

41
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:05.709
Formal writing.

42
00:02:06.717 --> 00:02:08.995
Formal writing means a serious style.

43
00:02:09.583 --> 00:02:10.666
Formal writing.

44
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.879
Your turn. Say: Formal writing.

45
00:02:16.733 --> 00:02:17.920
Formal writing.

46
00:02:18.733 --> 00:02:22.036
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.883 --> 00:02:25.312
Visal, which connector adds a new idea?

48
00:02:26.417 --> 00:02:40.684
Furthermore, moreover and in addition add an idea: The plan is cheap. Furthermore, it is fast. Consequently and therefore show result. Nevertheless and however show contrast.

49
00:02:41.783 --> 00:02:43.168
How do we punctuate them?

50
00:02:44.283 --> 00:02:57.094
At the start of a sentence, a connector takes a comma: Nevertheless, we continued. Between two clauses we use a semicolon before it: It rained; nevertheless, we played.

51
00:02:58.183 --> 00:02:59.463
Why do they matter?

52
00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:13.631
They give cohesion, so the reader can follow your argument. But use them carefully: too many make writing heavy. On the other hand compares two options, and consequently shows a result.

53
00:03:14.767 --> 00:03:16.128
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:16.983 --> 00:03:22.083
Grammar focus: Discourse connectors: addition, contrast, result.

55
00:03:22.383 --> 00:03:23.604
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:24.317 --> 00:03:27.294
The plan is cheap. Furthermore, it is fast.

57
00:03:28.183 --> 00:03:30.903
It rained; nevertheless, we played.

58
00:03:31.817 --> 00:03:34.759
He did not study. Consequently, he failed.

59
00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:45.602
Addition: furthermore, moreover, in addition. Contrast: nevertheless, however, on the other hand. Result: consequently, therefore. Put a comma after the connector.

60
00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:50.303
Be careful! Don't say: It rained, nevertheless we played.

61
00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:54.858
Say: It rained; nevertheless, we played.

62
00:03:55.158 --> 00:03:57.042
Use a semicolon and comma.

63
00:03:57.833 --> 00:04:00.474
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:02.674
Linking Ideas.

65
00:04:02.974 --> 00:04:06.683
The new system is cheap. Furthermore, it is easy to use.

66
00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:10.537
It rained heavily; nevertheless, we played the match.

67
00:04:11.533 --> 00:04:15.347
He did not study. Consequently, he failed the exam.

68
00:04:16.333 --> 00:04:19.157
On the other hand, the old system is more familiar.

69
00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:23.060
Good cohesion helps the reader follow your argument.

70
00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:28.377
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:29.217 --> 00:04:31.321
The idea is good. blank, it is cheap.

72
00:04:31.621 --> 00:04:35.611
A, Furthermore. B, Nevertheless. C, Consequently.

73
00:04:39.167 --> 00:04:41.085
The answer is A: Furthermore.

74
00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:43.971
He was ill. blank, he went to work.

75
00:04:44.271 --> 00:04:47.948
A, Moreover. B, Nevertheless. C, Therefore.

76
00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.639
The answer is B: Nevertheless.

77
00:04:54.783 --> 00:04:56.655
She didn't study. blank, she failed.

78
00:04:56.955 --> 00:05:01.015
A, Consequently. B, However. C, In addition.

79
00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:07.054
The answer is A: Consequently.

80
00:05:08.217 --> 00:05:09.880
Which shows contrast?

81
00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:14.135
A, on the other hand. B, moreover. C, in addition.

82
00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.967
The answer is A: on the other hand.

83
00:05:21.117 --> 00:05:24.347
According to the reading, what does good cohesion help?

84
00:05:24.647 --> 00:05:28.358
A, the reader. B, the writer. C, the teacher.

85
00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:33.934
The answer is A: the reader.

86
00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:38.018
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:38.883 --> 00:05:42.276
Write two sentences connected with a formal discourse connector.

88
00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:52.595
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:52.895 --> 00:06:00.438
Public transport is cheap. Moreover, it reduces traffic in the city. I use moreover to add an idea and a comma after it.

90
00:06:00.738 --> 00:06:02.633
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:03.517 --> 00:06:09.559
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and discourse connectors: addition, contrast, result.

92
00:06:09.859 --> 00:06:15.159
Today's value is media literacy. Ask who made the message, and why, before you believe it.

93
00:06:15.459 --> 00:06:18.099
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

94
00:06:18.399 --> 00:06:21.888
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

